      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense, the buffering capacity of the gluten is a good point. I noticed that even with consistent temps, the acidity still feels almost... chaotic, like it's behaving in ways that don't follow a linear progression. Is there something else in the microbial ecosystem that could be causing those sudden, sharp spikes in acidity? Like, are there certain microbes that act more aggressively than others when the conditions aren't perfect?",
